{"name":"Cosmopolitan","hex":"#528bab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cosmopolitan","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Inclusive; affecting the whole world.","Composed of people from all over the world."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cosmopolitan person; a cosmopolite.","A cocktail containing vodka, triple sec, lime juice and cranberry juice."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cosmopolitan"}],"entries":[{"title":"Global citizenship","blocks":[{"text":"Global citizenship is a form of transnationality, specifically the idea that one's identity transcends geography or political borders and that responsibilities or rights are derived from membership in a broader global class of \"humanity\". This does not mean that such a person denounces or waives their nationality or other, more local identities, but that such identities are given \"second place\" to their membership in a global community. Extended, the idea leads to questions about the state of global society in the age of globalization."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_citizenship"},{"title":"Cosmopolitanism","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmopolitanism is the idea that all human beings are members of a single community. Its adherents are known as cosmopolitan or cosmopolite. Cosmopolitanism is both prescriptive and aspirational, believing humans can and should be \"world citizens\" in a \"universal community\". The idea encompasses different dimensions and avenues of community, such as promoting universal moral standards, establishing global political structures, or developing a platform for mutual cultural expression and tolerance."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmopolitanism"},{"title":"Cosmopolitan (cocktail)","blocks":[{"text":"A cosmopolitan, or, informally, a cosmo, is a cocktail made with vodka, Cointreau, cranberry juice, and freshly squeezed or sweetened lime juice. The traditional garnish is a lime slice but a twist or wedge can be used instead. Other variations substitute lemon or orange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Cosmopolitan_%285076906532%29.jpg/330px-Cosmopolitan_%285076906532%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmopolitan_(cocktail)"},{"title":"Cosmopolitan (magazine)","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmopolitan is an American quarterly women's fashion and entertainment magazine first published in New York City in March 1886 as a family magazine; it was later transformed into a literary magazine and, since 1965, has become a women's magazine. Cosmopolitan is one of the best-selling magazines."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/54/US_Cosmopolitan_Fall_2025.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmopolitan_(magazine)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Waterhouse-Diogenes.jpg/500px-Waterhouse-Diogenes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Waterhouse-Diogenes.jpg/1280px-Waterhouse-Diogenes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Waterhouse-Diogenes.jpg/500px-Waterhouse-Diogenes.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Diogenes by John William Waterhouse, 1882","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWaterhouse-Diogenes.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Cosmopolitan-FC-November-1917.jpg/500px-Cosmopolitan-FC-November-1917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Cosmopolitan-FC-November-1917.jpg/1280px-Cosmopolitan-FC-November-1917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Cosmopolitan-FC-November-1917.jpg/500px-Cosmopolitan-FC-November-1917.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"November 1917 issue of Cosmopolitan cover by Harrison Fisher","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACosmopolitan-FC-November-1917.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Cosmopolitan.jpg/500px-Cosmopolitan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Cosmopolitan.jpg/500px-Cosmopolitan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cosmopolitan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACosmopolitan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/CosmopolitanMagazineMarch1894.jpg/330px-CosmopolitanMagazineMarch1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/CosmopolitanMagazineMarch1894.jpg/330px-CosmopolitanMagazineMarch1894.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACosmopolitanMagazineMarch1894.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Jeffrey_Epstein%2C_27.jpg/500px-Jeffrey_Epstein%2C_27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Jeffrey_Epstein%2C_27.jpg/1280px-Jeffrey_Epstein%2C_27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Jeffrey_Epstein%2C_27.jpg/500px-Jeffrey_Epstein%2C_27.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jeffrey Epstein was the magazine's \"Bachelor of the month\" in the July 1980 issue.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJeffrey_Epstein%2C_27.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/COSMOPOLITAN_magazine_at_The_Brandery_Summer_Edition_2010.jpg/500px-COSMOPOLITAN_magazine_at_The_Brandery_Summer_Edition_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/COSMOPOLITAN_magazine_at_The_Brandery_Summer_Edition_2010.jpg/1280px-COSMOPOLITAN_magazine_at_The_Brandery_Summer_Edition_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/COSMOPOLITAN_magazine_at_The_Brandery_Summer_Edition_2010.jpg/500px-COSMOPOLITAN_magazine_at_The_Brandery_Summer_Edition_2010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cosmopolitan stand at The Brandery fashion show (Barcelona, 2010)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACOSMOPOLITAN_magazine_at_The_Brandery_Summer_Edition_2010.jpg"}],"sounds":{"cosmopolitan":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4b/En-us-cosmopolitan.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/4/4b/En-us-cosmopolitan.ogg/En-us-cosmopolitan.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5a/En-au-cosmopolitan.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/5/5a/En-au-cosmopolitan.ogg/En-au-cosmopolitan.ogg.mp3"}]}}}